<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Adil</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1200–<a href="/years/1218">1218</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Adil was the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> and sultan of the Ayyubid realm from 1200 to 1218. After Saladin's death in 1193, rival heirs fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, and al-Adil's patient statesmanship allowed him to reunify most of the realm by 1200. His descendants ruled the main Ayyubid branches, though the family remained prone to internal division.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-adil.jpg" alt="al-Adil" width="320" height="301" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al_Adil_Sayf_al_Din_Abu_Bakr_Muhammad_I._As_Governor_in_Mesopotamia,_1194-1199._Mayafariqin_mint._Dated_AH_591_(1194-1195_AD).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
